es that  we should add more countries to join g20  given to many countries that have  expanded their economic capacities have  advanced their economic growth and so on  and so forth but the problem now is if  we talk about ukraine and russia that  you know the concerns are not coming  from the high level government or  presidents or prime minister of western  countries but so far what i heard from  the other engagement group and working  groups that we have under the umbrella  of g20 many businesses many other  parties and stakeholders are not  demanded to  also uh excluded while shy in the  negotiation in the discussion of g20  this is a big problem again we cannot  underestimate this right and i think you  know having other member states are not  solving the problem whether we should  include russia or not but again also in  other ways exposing russia from g20 will  not also help solving the economic  problems that we have so that's why i  understand that the government of  indonesia as the president of g20 is  trying to be carefully thinking about  the best solutions to this crisis  can indonesia thomas actually use its  leadership to resolve the problems  yes indonesia has a political capital  not only by its free and active foreign  policy so what i suggest the government  to the foreign ministry is that we  should extend all of the product  capitals that we have and then trying to  solve this of course the particle  problem is number one but i agree with  everybody especially the economist that  the economic impacts are now inevitable  to this g20 member states so that's why  we should thinking hard and also trying  hard to solve this immediately elizabeth  a final word to you on the issue of the  g20 i mean not to single out poland but  there are countries other countries as  well such as  nigeria and thailand who reportedly all  have higher gdps than current g20  members so is it time that the g20  uh opened up its membership or or  reforms and starts to include other  countries what's your take on this  i certainly think that those things  should be under consideration and  discussion at this time um in addition  to the idea of you know should it be  based strictly on economic signs or  should there be other factors in such as  are you a good player in this uh you  know integrated economic international  system that we have but yes i mean  russia particularly after this set of  sanctions is no longer really at that at  that size and level so um i believe that  we should be careful about just rapidly  expanding size and reaction to the  situation uh because you have uh the i  mean it's an economic body that does  have an important kind of diplomatic  role in negotiating these issues but  they should certainly consider  the fact of which which other countries  might play a more positive um and  affirmative role in this body and if  there are countries that are creating  the types of economic issues out there  such as russia with its aggressive war  in ukraine right now then we should uh  we should consider whether or not  they're the types of countries that are  helping us resolve these problems are  causing them all right on that note  we'll leave it there thank you so much  for joining us elizabeth shackleford  daniel bochkov and thomas no sueno too  thank you so much  thanks for watching you can see the  program again anytime by visiting our  website aljazeera.com for further  discussion you can go to our facebook  page that's facebook.com forward slash  aj inside story you can join the  conversation on twitter as well our  handle is aj inside story for myself and  the whole team here in doha thanks for  watching and bye for now  [Music]
 

